## Check the implementation

Test long service names, keyboard focus, account names, menu expansion and small-screen wrapping. The example navigation uses in-frame destinations; real links must retain native Home Assistant routes.

Use the [civica accessibility checks](../accessibility/testing.html) and compare the rendered result in light and dark modes, Vivid and Muted tones, and at 320 CSS pixels. The example markup is a starting point; a theme alone does not add its application logic.

## Source and related guidance

[NHS header](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/header) informs the component choice and interaction guidance. The examples use shared GOV.UK primitives or original civica markup, Arial typography and original household examples. NHS logos and service identity are not used.

